#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197978 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of a Rod About the Origin"}] :question/id #uuid "cb13bd5e-ec8a-5e5c-a45f-d710ced8c3ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-12473" :question/problem "The thin rod below has the mass density function $\\lambda (x) = (x+4)\\,\\textrm{kg/m}$. Find the moment of the rod about the origin.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4167/Source/Images/ac2d4ddc8a114f8f9399775fec32db1a.png)" :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda(x)$ for\n\n$$\na \\leq x \\leq b\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\nM_O = \\int_a^b x\\, \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x) = x+4, \\qquad a=0, \\qquad b=3\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM_{O} &= ∫_{0}^{3}x \\cdot (x + 4)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{3}x^{2} + 4xdx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{x^{3}}{3} + 2x^{2}]_{0}^{3} \\\\\n&= (\\frac{3^{3}}{3} + 2 \\cdot 3^{2}) - 0 \\\\\n&= 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required moment is $27\\,\\textrm{kg}\\cdot \\textrm{m}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197979 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass of a Rod"}] :question/id #uuid "4ebe8c87-95ba-58e2-b5d4-1bb19f231dc1" :question/math-academy-id "e-12474" :question/problem "The thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x) = x^3$. Given that the rod's mass is $4$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4167/Source/Images/8c63fd7d44dfaf371d96c176253bfc52.png)" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval\n\n$$\na \\leq x \\leq b\n$$\n\nwhose mass density function is $\\lambda(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\int_a^b \\lambda (x) \\: \\textrm{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n- $\\displaystyle M_O = \\int_a^b \\, x\\lambda (x) \\: \\textrm{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O$.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x) = x^3, \\qquad a=0, \\qquad b=2\n$$\n\nSo, the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM_{O} &= ∫_{0}^{2}x \\cdot x^{3}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}x^{4}dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{1}{5}x^{5}]_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}(32 - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{32}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overline{x}= \\dfrac{M_O}{m} = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{32}{5}\\right)}{4} = \\dfrac{8}{5}\n$$\n\nNote that this result makes intuitive sense. Since $\\lambda$ is an increasing function of $x$, we would expect the center of mass to be located closer to the right endpoint and further from the left endpoint."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197980 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Mass of a Thin Rod"}] :question/id #uuid "5c469b72-7ee3-5084-be63-2b7e62b42146" :question/math-academy-id "e-12475" :question/problem "The thin rod below has the mass density function $\\lambda(x) =2x\\, \\textrm{kg/m}$, where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4167/Source/Images/ab9b1a56295dd675dc0079231bebfe76.png)" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the $x$-axis over the interval\n\n$$\na \\leq x \\leq b\n$$\n\nif $\\lambda(x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by\n\n$$\nm = \\int_a^b \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x) = 2x, \\qquad a=1, \\qquad b=3\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= ∫_{1}^{3}2xdx \\\\\n&= [x^{2}]_{1}^{3} \\\\\n&= 3^{2} - 1^{2} \\\\\n&= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\textrm{kg}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of a Rod About the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db0b873f-0cf1-5894-ba1f-75e8421f48d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194292} {:answer/id #uuid "e61179f0-cd6a-57f2-a57b-4656a9ae0621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194293} {:answer/id #uuid "403b306a-988f-5a33-bf11-5f7d518cab2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194294} {:answer/id #uuid "48af1c9c-40da-507c-a737-df47585d3d6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194295} {:answer/id #uuid "57685e2b-b408-55c6-818e-c851ed20d9e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e61179f0-cd6a-57f2-a57b-4656a9ae0621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194293} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb35b049-8ee1-5a0d-9117-293f22cd3c86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194291}] :question/id #uuid "3ae9b639-ddf7-5a21-a2c9-715cb70d087a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162948" :question/problem "A thin rod with mass density function $λ(x) = 4x^{2}$, measured in $kg/m$, is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1 \\le x \\le 2$, where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass of a Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aed4dff9-c500-59ad-b94a-8e2b32b21454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194304} {:answer/id #uuid "c0dde479-38d3-5595-9980-463ae5d6d87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194305} {:answer/id #uuid "f210d88f-b395-5391-be7d-70ba0d5628b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194306} {:answer/id #uuid "29e4ae9d-1bdb-566d-a4e4-918e4eda5351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194307} {:answer/id #uuid "423a1633-2ba6-54b9-9fd4-7778b05e9052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29e4ae9d-1bdb-566d-a4e4-918e4eda5351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194307} :answer-field/id #uuid "063a6123-d8f9-5157-acb7-3c575af4c824" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194303}] :question/id #uuid "2b48c642-16a8-5d6a-818c-93071a473cf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-162957" :question/problem "Consider a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $0 \\le x \\le 2$ whose mass density function is $λ(x) = 3x$. Given that the rod's mass is $6$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?"}]}
